            <ArticleTitle>Inclusion body myopathy and Paget disease is linked to a novel mutation in the VCP gene.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1304-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Mutations in the valosin-containing protein (VCP) on chromosome 9p13-p12 were recently found to be associated with hereditary inclusion body myopathy, Paget disease of the bone, and frontotemporal dementia (IBMPFD). We identified a novel missense mutation in the VCP gene (R159H; 688G&gt;A) segregating with this disease in an Austrian family of four affected siblings, who exhibited progressive proximal myopathy and Paget disease of the bone but without clinical signs of dementia.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
